          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Sacred rest grounded in God’s completed creation, commonly understood typologically as pointing to the believer’s rest in Christ and ultimately to eternal or eschatological rest with God.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Genesis 2:2–3 — God rests on and sanctifies the seventh day after completing creation.\",\"Exodus 20:8–11 — Sabbath rest is patterned on God’s creation rest.\",\"Deuteronomy 5:12–15 — Sabbath also commemorates Israel’s deliverance from slavery.\",\"Hebrews 4:1–11 — Sabbath rest is applied to entering God’s rest through faith and to a rest still awaiting God’s people.\",\"Colossians 2:16–17 — Sabbaths are described as a shadow whose substance belongs to Christ.\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The Sabbath is primarily the covenant sign marking Israel as God’s sanctified people, rather than chiefly a symbol of inward or heavenly rest.\",\"basis\":[\"Exodus 31:12–17\",\"Ezekiel 20:12, 20\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The Sabbath symbolizes liberation from oppression, humane treatment of workers and animals, and social equality before God.\",\"basis\":[\"Deuteronomy 5:12–15\",\"Exodus 23:10–12\",\"Isaiah 58:13–14\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The seventh-day Sabbath remains a continuing literal creation ordinance and divine command for Christians, while also signifying creation, redemption, and sanctification.\",\"basis\":[\"Genesis 2:2–3\",\"Exodus 20:8–11\",\"Mark 2:27–28\",\"Luke 4:16\",\"Hebrews 4:9\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"The Sabbath is typologically transferred to or fulfilled in the Christian Lord’s Day, Sunday, which commemorates Christ’s resurrection and anticipates eternal rest.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 28:1–6\",\"Acts 20:7\",\"1 Corinthians 16:2\",\"Revelation 1:10\",\"Hebrews 4:9–11\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The Sabbath foreshadows a future millennial ‘seventh age’ of history or a thousand-year messianic rest.\",\"basis\":[\"Psalm 90:4\",\"2 Peter 3:8\",\"Revelation 20:1–6\",\"Hebrews 4:9–11\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":false,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"Christian interpretation has a strong dominant association between the Sabbath and divine rest—creation rest, rest in Christ, and final rest—but no single precise symbolic interpretation is settled across traditions. Disagreement especially concerns whether the Sabbath is fulfilled in Christ, transferred to Sunday, or remains binding as the literal seventh day.\"}"
        }
      ],
